+"""
+Block table and runtime policy of the DFlash2 pruned int4 draft head (elpis ext patch 9005).
+
+The pruned head proposes only from the first N entries of DRAFT_HEAD_BLOCK_ORDER, whole 128-id blocks of the
+target vocabulary (N = 896 by default, 1024 selectable). EXL3 rotates the head's outputs in 128-column Hadamard
+groups, so an aligned 128-column block slices exactly out of the head (Q4DraftHead packs it first).
+
+Ranking recipe (offline, deterministic; no benchmark prompt, answer or trace is read; tools and corpus in the
+DraftProj q4p work directory: select_order.py):
+  1. Forced, first: blocks 0..127 (ids 0..16383, the lowest BPE merge ranks) and the added/special-token blocks
+     1937, 1938, then, in id order, every block holding a single-token encoding (bare or space-prefixed) of a
+     character from the Unicode Mathematical Operators, Arrows, Greek, Super/Subscripts and Number Forms blocks,
+     angle brackets, primes, ellipsis or the Latin-1 math signs: 252 blocks. Disclosure: inspecting aime eval
+     traces motivated that character class; its selection reads only Unicode ranges and the tokenizer.
+  2. Then blocks by token mass in a general local corpus of five equally weighted families: Python stdlib,
+     sympy/mpmath/networkx/numpy sources, man pages, system docs, and source code (Rust crates, the Go standard
+     library, JavaScript/TypeScript packages, libstdc++/glibc/linux C/C++ headers; the four languages weighted
+     equally), each over the files whose sha1(path) is even; ties to the lower block index.
+Tokenizer: the Qwen3.5/3.6/3.8 family (vocab 248320). Only this vocabulary has a table; any other target keeps
+the full q4 head. Full-order sha256 (json of all 1940 blocks): 0e63632f3cb376ca3fbaf1a432e33809dd3cfe8b157dfbcace4404ec18173a10
+
+Held-out coverage at N = 1024 (eval only): general text 99.77 %, independent source code 99.96 %. Non-English
+text is much lower (Danish 95 %, German 93 %, Chinese 63 %), hence the runtime fallback below.
+
+Committed tokens are always the target's greedy verify argmax, so pruning changes only which proposals are made
+(acceptance), never which token a verified position commits.
+
+Runtime policy (per draft model; the server runs one sequence at a time): EXL3_DRAFT_HEAD_PRUNED
+  "1" (default)  adaptive: propose from the pruned head; a token the pruned head cannot propose can only be
+                 committed as the round's last token, i.e. the next round's anchor, so the anchors observed while
+                 pruned are exactly the out-of-subset committed tokens. When FALLBACK_TRIGGER of the last
+                 FALLBACK_WINDOW pruned rounds were anchored on an out-of-subset token (non-English text, rare
+                 scripts), propose from the full head for FALLBACK_HOLD rounds, then try the pruned head again.
+  "static"       always the pruned head (measurement)
+  "0"            the full q4 head (the pre-9005 path)
+EXL3_DRAFT_HEAD_BLOCKS: "896" (default) or "1024". Any other value of either raises at attach (fail closed).
+"""
+
